{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":429696,"duration_api_ms":427032,"ttft_ms":5625,"ttft_stream_ms":2047,"time_to_request_ms":146,"num_turns":15,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n  \"summary\": \"The repo has no CI/CD pipeline, no vercel.json, and no existing health/status endpoint. Infra scope for status-page is narrow: decide and wire how 'backend version' and 'current application environment' are sourced into runtime env vars (Vercel system env vars / git SHA), ensure the status endpoint is not cached or secret-leaking, and flag that there is currently no automated pipeline enforcing the required tests.\",\n  \"areas_affected\": [\n    \"Vercel project environment variable configuration (VERCEL_ENV, VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA exposure)\",\n    \".env.example documentation of any new public env vars\",\n    \"Runtime/caching configuration for the new status API route (no-store, dynamic rendering)\",\n    \"Absence of CI/CD workflow (.github/workflows) that would run npm run verify on PRs\"\n  ],\n  \"proposed_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-1-define-version-source\",\n      \"description\": \"Decide the source of truth for 'backend version': package.json version vs. Vercel's auto-injected VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA (short SHA) vs. a build-time generated version file. No versioning/tagging scheme exists in this repo today (package.json is still 0.1.0, no CHANGELOG/git tags found).\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infra\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-2-expose-env-vars\",\n      \"description\": \"Wire the chosen version source and the current environment (production/preview/development) into env vars readable by the status endpoint at runtime. Vercel auto-sets VERCEL_ENV and VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA server-side; enabling 'Automatically expose System Environment Variables' in the Vercel dashboard (or manually mapping to NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed vars) is an infra/dashboard action outside this codebase.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infra\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"infra-1-define-version-source\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-3-document-env-vars\",\n      \"description\": \"If any new env var is introduced for this feature, add it to .env.example with a comment, consistent with the existing pattern there.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infra\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"infra-2-expose-env-vars\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-4-runtime-caching-contract\",\n      \"description\": \"Specify that the status API route must opt out of caching (force-dynamic / Cache-Control: no-store) so it always reflects live state, and must not be blocked by any auth middleware/rewrites that would prevent external monitoring from reaching it.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"backend\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-5-ci-gap-flag\",\n      \"description\": \"Repo currently has no .github/workflows or any CI pipeline — 'include tests' only guarantees tests exist, not that they run automatically on PRs. Optionally add a CI workflow invoking npm run verify. This is broader than the status-page feature itself and needs explicit authorization per AGENTS.md before implementation.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infra\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contracts\": [\n    \"Env var contract: a server-readable APP_VERSION value (source decided in infra-1) must be available wherever the status endpoint executes.\",\n    \"Env var contract: a server-readable APP_ENV/environment label (production | preview | development) must be available at runtime, ideally derived from Vercel's VERCEL_ENV rather than duplicated.\",\n    \"Response-caching contract: the status endpoint route must disable caching/CDN/edge caching so the status page is never stale.\",\n    \"No secrets (e.g. Supabase service role key, DIRECT_CONN_STRING) may be read or echoed by the status endpoint — only public/non-sensitive identifiers.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"Publicly exposing a full git commit SHA or detailed version/environment info is a minor information-disclosure risk that could help an attacker fingerprint the deployment — recommend truncating/limiting detail.\",\n    \"If 'API availability' implies live-pinging Supabase or another backend dependency, a slow/hanging dependency could make the status endpoint itself hang on Vercel's serverless/edge runtime without an explicit timeout — needs a bounded timeout, which is a config concern even though the check logic is backend-owned.\",\n    \"No CI currently enforces tests or verify on PRs, so 'include tests' for this feature won't be automatically gated unless a workflow is added (see infra-5) — flagging so the team doesn't assume tests are enforced.\"\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    \"Not infra-owned directly, but infra should confirm `npm run verify` (lint, typecheck, build) still passes once the new route/page files exist, since Vercel's build must succeed for deployment.\",\n    \"Recommend the test suite (owned by backend/frontend) assert the status endpoint reports the expected environment label per Vercel environment (production/preview/development), since infra defines what values are possible.\"\n  ],\n  \"questions_or_unknowns\": [\n    \"Should 'backend version' be package.json's semantic version, a git SHA, or a build timestamp? This repo has no existing versioning/release convention.\",\n    \"Should the status endpoint perform a live connectivity check against Supabase ('API availability'), or just report static build/environment info with no external dependency? This determines whether infra needs to worry about timeouts/secrets for an outbound check.\",\n    \"Is an unauthenticated, publicly reachable status page acceptable, or should it be gated/rate-limited given this is a B2B marketplace app?\",\n    \"Should this task include adding a CI workflow (none exists today), or is that explicitly out of scope for status-page?\"\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"42f834ee-94dc-48bb-82d7-6396df6c5627","total_cost_usd":0.4908693,"usage":{"input_tokens":17818,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32098,"cache_read_input_tokens":464591,"output_tokens":7030,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32098,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2061,"cache_read_input_tokens":56745,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2433},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":17818,"outputTokens":7030,"cacheReadInputTokens":464591,"cacheCreationInputTokens":32098,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4908693,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01EJj9GYnG9XMRkGPSJHNVWP","tool_input":{"command":"rm -f \"C:\\Users\\HMN\\.claude\\plans\\you-are-participating-in-mellow-hamster.md\"","description":"Remove placeholder plan file since this role must not write a plan file"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"5f7fccd8-4348-48ac-afe3-70adcaabe0f5"}
